<div>
    <p>Each row is a named backup configuration (which of database/code/storage to include, a cron expression for reference, and how many archives to retain). Click "Run now" on a row to queue a <code>RunBackupJob</code> immediately, or run <code>php artisan backup:run {id?}</code> (omit the id to run every configured backup) from an external cron — this module does not wire its own scheduler, matching the old project.</p>
    <p>Database dumps use <code>spatie/db-dumper</code> (MySQL/MariaDB and PostgreSQL). Code/storage backups are plain zip archives of the app root (excluding <code>vendor</code>, <code>node_modules</code>, <code>storage</code>, <code>.git</code>, <code>.idea</code>, <code>scratch</code>, <code>bootstrap/cache</code>) and <code>storage/app/public</code> respectively.</p>
    <p>Archives are uploaded to the disk/path configured on this module's own "Settings" screen (<code>storage_disk</code>/<code>storage_path</code>) and the oldest ones beyond <code>max_backups</code> are deleted automatically after each run. The <a href="{{ route('nexus.module.action', ['module' => 'Restore', 'action' => 'index']) }}">Restore</a> module reads these same settings to find the archives.</p>
</div>
